# Global Safety Invariants

Full detail lives in `AGENTS.md`, `PRODUCT.md`, `docs/architecture.md`, and
accepted ADRs under `docs/adr/`, including [ADR 0014](../../docs/adr/0014-portfolio-product-reset.md).
This rule is the minimal always-on summary — read the scoped rule and
canonical docs relevant to your files before a non-trivial change.

- **`content/source/cv.yaml` is read-only fact.** Never edit it, "correct"
  it, or invent/infer a fact beyond what it states.
- **Facts vs. narrative.** Narrative framing, structure, and Spanish
  translation may be genuinely creative — never a mechanical mirror. But no
  new fact, metric, employer, user count, model result, or date may ever be
  invented anywhere on the site.
- **Clean-room only.** Never reuse, paraphrase, or infer proprietary Infosys
  "Agent Governance Framework" code/architecture/docs. Only reimplement
  public concepts (W3C DIDs/VCs, OPA/Rego, Merkle audit, OpenTelemetry) from
  public specs, cited under `content/public-sources/`.
- **Synthetic data only, forever.** No real visitor-submitted input is
  stored or logged anywhere. Canonical CV fields render only on
  portfolio/résumé routes and are never copied elsewhere.
- **Secrets never reach the client.** No API key in browser code, client
  bundles, or `PUBLIC_*`/`NEXT_PUBLIC_*`-style vars. Server-only;
  `.env.example` gets placeholders, never real values.
- **No fabricated photography.** No AI-generated photo of Diego, ever — only
  a deliberate, honest placeholder until a real one exists.
- **Honest project states.** A `planned` or `building` project must look and
  read as unfinished — never implied as shipped or verified.
- **No AI co-author trailers in commits.** Diego is the sole author of
  record.
- **Architecture is decided.** Follow `docs/architecture.md` and accepted
  ADRs. Do not reopen stack, deployment-target, provider-seam, or
  visual-direction choices without a superseding ADR.

If a requested change conflicts with any invariant above, stop and flag the
conflict instead of proceeding.
